WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.384 --> 00:00:05.024
Whether this is legally binding, or a
rulework like the one we see here, whether

2
00:00:05.024 --> 00:00:06.464
that is legally binding.

3
00:00:08.187 --> 00:00:10.928
The law is legally binding.

4
00:00:10.928 --> 00:00:14.848
Because these are machine-executable
interpretations of the law.

5
00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:20.372
Just as software today is a
machine-executable interpretation of the law.

6
00:00:20.372 --> 00:00:23.153
So the machine version isn't the law.

7
00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.154
The law is the law.

8
00:00:25.154 --> 00:00:29.115
And what we see is merely
an interpretation.

9
00:00:29.115 --> 00:00:33.995
And it only has that status, an
interpretation of the law, which can also be

10
00:00:33.995 --> 00:00:35.461
contested.

11
00:00:35.461 --> 00:00:39.621
The big difference is that it's an
interpretation you can inspect, that the

12
00:00:39.621 --> 00:00:44.221
implementer, the citizen, the business,
but also the legislature and the judiciary

13
00:00:44.221 --> 00:00:45.621
can all look at.

14
00:00:52.788 --> 00:00:56.148
And that interpretation is
transparent and published.
